Design: We can apply Test-Time Augmentation by averaging predictions on the original and horizontally‐flipped versions of each image at validation and inference. This simple modification acts like a two‐member ensemble without retraining and often boosts AUROC by making predictions more robust. We'll update the validation loop to average probabilities from the original and flipped inputs, and incorporate the same logic into the `predict()` function, leaving training unchanged.
