Design: We add a OneCycleLR scheduler so that the learning rate ramps up quickly at the start and anneals to zero by the end of training, which often yields better convergence and generalization. We keep the Adam optimizer’s max_lr at 1e-3, step the scheduler after every batch, and leave all other settings—including mixup, TTA, epochs, and transforms—unchanged. This atomic change requires minimal code edits but can produce a noticeable AUROC uplift. The validation loop and predict() function remain as before.
