-------------------------------
Design: I propose oversampling the minority (malignant) class during training via a WeightedRandomSampler so that each batch is more balanced, which can help the model learn better representations for the rare class and boost AUROC. We compute sample weights inversely proportional to class frequencies in the training set, use these in the sampler for the training DataLoader, and keep the rest of the pipeline—including mixup, random erasing, model, and two‐way TTA—invariant. This atomic change requires minimal edits but can improve performance on the positive class.
